`svg.renderSvg(state, elements)` — let me quickly check whether it uses jsdom-unsupported APIs. It iterates shapes, uses `elements.shapes` (an svg element created via createElementNS), sets `innerHTML`? Let me quickly check the render function in svg.ts. Actually — risk assessment: if svg rendering breaks in jsdom, the test will error during Chessground init. Let me skim the top of svg.ts.

